## 1. Setup

```bash
# Pin a release. Do not float on main for a team project.
uv tool install specify-cli --from git+https://github.com/github/spec-kit.git@vX.Y.Z

specify init workplaceiq-ui --integration copilot   # or claude, cursor, etc.
cd workplaceiq-ui

specify check                # verify tooling
specify integration list     # confirm your agent is wired up
```

**Figma MCP (VS Code):** `⌘⇧P` → `MCP: Add Server` → HTTP → `https://mcp.figma.com/mcp` → server ID `figma`.

Two facts that shape everything below:

- `get_design_context` returns a **React + Tailwind–shaped** representation regardless of your stack. It is design context, not production code. You must instruct the agent to translate it into Angular/React/whatever you actually use.
- `get_variable_defs` (design tokens) is a **desktop-server** tool. If you're on the remote server only, plan to export Figma variables to JSON manually instead.

Open the **project directory** in your editor, not its parent — otherwise the `/speckit.*` slash commands won't appear.

