## Phase 0 — Design intake (before any Spec Kit command)

Run these in a **plain agent chat**, not a slash command. You are building durable inputs,
not requirements yet.

### 0a. Frame index

> Using the Figma MCP server, run `get_metadata` on the WorkplaceIQ file to get the node map.
> Write `design/figma-sources.md` listing every top-level frame: frame name, node ID, page it
> lives on, and whether it is a primary screen, a state variant, or a component. Do not write
> code and do not describe visuals.

**Result — `design/figma-sources.md`:**

```markdown
# WorkplaceIQ Figma Source Index
File key: AbC123XyZ    Last synced: 2026-09-05

| Frame | Node ID | Page | Type |
|---|---|---|---|
| App Shell / Desktop | 12:400 | Foundations | Primary |
| Portfolio Overview / Desktop | 1204:5567 | Screens | Primary |
| Portfolio Overview / Empty | 1204:5612 | Screens | State variant |
| Portfolio Overview / Loading | 1204:5640 | Screens | State variant |
| Portfolio Overview / Error | 1204:5668 | Screens | State variant |
| Grant Detail / Desktop | 1310:2201 | Screens | Primary |
| KPI Tile | 88:120 | Components | Component |
| Data Table / Default | 88:340 | Components | Component |
```

Everything downstream references node IDs from this table. Node IDs survive renames; frame
names do not.

### 0b. Tokens

> Run `get_variable_defs` across the Foundations page and write the result to
> `design/tokens.json` as DTCG-format JSON. Group by colour, spacing, typography, radius,
> elevation. Preserve Figma's variable names exactly — do not rename or "clean up".

If you're on the remote MCP server only, export Figma variables to JSON from the Figma UI
instead and commit the same file.

### 0c. Design system rules

> Run `create_design_system_rules` and save the output to `design/design-system-rules.md`.

This is a file the Figma MCP generates specifically so the agent knows how to map design
system concepts into your codebase. It's the highest-leverage single file for visual fidelity.
Edit it afterwards to name your real component library and framework.

### 0d. Screenshots

> For each primary and state-variant frame in `design/figma-sources.md`, run `get_screenshot`
> and save to `design/screens/<slug>.png`.

Screenshots are supplemental context — a screenshot combined with the structured code output
performs better than either alone, because imagery carries design *intent* that metadata misses.

### 0e. Screen inventory — the most important file in Phase 0

> For each primary frame in `design/figma-sources.md`, run `get_design_context` and write
> `design/screen-inventory.md`. For every screen record: purpose in one line; every distinct
> data element visible with its label and what it represents in business terms; every filter
> or control; every drill-down or navigation target; which state variants exist. Record only
> what is on the canvas. Do not infer requirements, do not propose components, do not write
> code. Put anything ambiguous under "## Questions for business".

